MIPLIB2017-Infeas
=================

WHAT THIS NOTICE COVERS

What is published here is not all under one set of terms, and this project is
not in a position to put it under one.

  Ours, under CC BY-SA 4.0 to the extent we hold rights in it. The derivation
  of each linear program, the `.meta.json` sidecars, the published indexes, the
  website and the code that builds it. The qualifier is meant: a matrix, a row
  count and a checksum are facts, and facts carry no copyright. Where none
  subsists the licence grants nothing. Its full text follows this notice.

  The instance data, adapted from MIPLIB 2017. Copyright in each original
  instance rests with its contributor, not with this project. What those
  contributors granted is set out under SOURCE INSTANCES below. This project
  asserts no licence over the instance data beyond what they granted, and for
  130 of the 262 source instances nothing was granted at all.

  MIPLIB's own text, quoted not licensed. Each instance page shows the source
  instance's description, submitter, group and tags as MIPLIB publishes them,
  and `metadata/miplib_meta.json` holds the same fields. That text is Zuse
  Institute Berlin's, carries no licence on miplib.zib.de, and is reproduced
  here as attributed quotation. This project does not place it under CC BY-SA
  4.0 and has no standing to.

  The typefaces, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. The site serves subsets
  of IBM Plex, copyright IBM Corp., cut to the glyphs these pages set. The OFL
  counts removing glyphs as a Modified Version and reserves the name "Plex"
  for the original, so they are published as Infeas Sans, Infeas Serif and
  Infeas Mono; `scripts/subset_fonts.py` produced them from the upstream
  release. Their licence travels with them, in `fonts/LICENSE.txt`, both in
  this repository and in every built copy of the site.

