SOURCE INSTANCES

262 MIPLIB 2017 instances are adapted here, and their terms are not uniform.
What follows is what MIPLIB's own records say. It was checked against ZIB's
submission repository, https://git.zib.de/miplib2017/submissions, which holds
one `meta.yml` per submission recording the licence its submitter chose.

131 source instances carry CC BY-SA 4.0.
  Submitted to MIPLIB 2017 through its submission form, whose licence field
  defaulted to CC BY-SA 4.0; their `meta.yml` records `license: cc-license`.
  ShareAlike obliges adapted material to carry the same licence, so the linear
  programs derived from these are published under CC BY-SA 4.0.

1 source instance carries BSD 3-Clause.
  `adult-max5features`, submitted by Berk Ustun, is the one contributor who
  chose other terms: its `meta.yml` records `license: other` with
  `other-license: BSD`. BSD 3-Clause permits redistribution of modified work
  provided the copyright notice, conditions and disclaimer are reproduced, so
  they are reproduced in full below and the derived file
  `adult-max5features_if.mps.gz` is distributed under those same terms.

  BSD 3-Clause License

  Copyright (c) 2017, Berk Ustun
  All rights reserved.

  Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without
  modification, are permitted provided that the following conditions are met:

  * Redistributions of source code must retain the above copyright notice, this
    list of conditions and the following disclaimer.

  * Redistributions in binary form must reproduce the above copyright notice,
    this list of conditions and the following disclaimer in the documentation
    and/or other materials provided with the distribution.

  * Neither the name of the copyright holder nor the names of its
    contributors may be used to endorse or promote products derived from
    this software without specific prior written permission.

  THIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED BY THE COPYRIGHT HOLDERS AND CONTRIBUTORS "AS IS"
  AND ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE
  IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE ARE
  DISCLAIMED. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER OR CONTRIBUTORS BE LIABLE
  FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL
  DAMAGES (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR
  SERVICES; LOSS OF USE, DATA, OR PROFITS; OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) HOWEVER
  CAUSED AND ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY,
  OR TORT (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE
  OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.

130 source instances carry no licence of record.
  These were not submitted to MIPLIB 2017. MIPLIB says so itself: each of their
  instance pages carries a provenance note, and the 130 divide as

     74   "Imported from the MIPLIB2010 submissions."
     55   "Imported from MIPLIB2010."
      1   "Imported from MIPLIB2003."

  In ZIB's submission repository all of them sit in one directory,
  `submission2010/`, whose `meta.yml` leaves `license`, `other-license`,
  `owner`, `name` and `email` all empty.

  MIPLIB 2017 scoped its licensing requirement to what was newly submitted to
  it. Gleixner et al. (§2.1) write that "all contributions were required to be
  submitted under a license" and that "the default license was chosen to be the
  Creative Commons CC BY-SA 4.0 license" of the 3,670 instances submitted to
  MIPLIB 2017; the 2,051 older instances were added, in their words, "keeping
  their original submission information intact". MIPLIB 2010 predates that
  requirement, so no licence accompanied them and none was applied afterwards.
  Neither MIPLIB nor anyone else has placed these instances under CC BY-SA 4.0,
  and this project does not do so either.

  They are redistributed here on the footing ZIB distributes them on: the
  source instance is named, its contributor is credited, the changes made are
  recorded, and no licence is asserted over them. Anyone holding rights in one
  of these instances who would rather it were not republished should open an
  issue at https://github.com/MIT-Lu-Lab/MIPLIB2017-Infeas and it will be withdrawn.

  The 130 source instances concerned, from which 172 of the 334 published
  linear programs derive:

